<title>USA: First Federal Q3 declines, inc charge.</title>
<headline>First Federal Q3 declines, inc charge.</headline>
<dateline>EAST HARTFORD, Conn. 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr		 $0.09		    $0.48</p>
<p> Net		 238			1,277</p>
<p> Net interest inc5,749		    5,038</p>
<p> Total assets    942,648		  866,054</p>
<p> Avg shrs	  2,679		    2,652</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers) Full company name is First Federal Savings and Loan Association of East Hartford</p>
<p>NOTE: Third quarter 1996 excludes a one-time special assessment of $3.1 million to recapitalize the Savings Association Insurance Fund, as mandated by U.S. law. The bank said as a result of the legislation, its deposit insurance premiums would also be reduced by $1 million a year starting in 1997.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
